{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270602",
      "title": "State Scheduling & Batching",
      "sourceHash": "ddc84ede3ba8351fa98c6db1c8e7b21670f234da48de55b77e183ecb1f4cb01c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.19,
          "en": "So now at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "we're almost done for this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "but there's one last state related concept here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "which I also want to explore together with you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 16.35,
          "en": "And that's how state updates are in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.35,
          "end": 19.023,
          "en": "scheduled and executed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "Now, I did mention earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "that when you call a state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "like setChosenCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "the state update will be scheduled by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "It will not be executed instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 38.73,
          "en": "And that's why if you console log the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 43.23,
          "en": "right after updating it, you will not get the new state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.23,
          "end": 45.183,
          "en": "but instead the old state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "And it's a common misconception that people think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "that they update the state in one line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 56.01,
          "en": "and then in the next line they can use the updated state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 58.08,
          "en": "This won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "If I open the console here and clear this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 62.88,
          "en": "and I set a new state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.88,
          "end": 65.98,
          "en": "You see here I'm getting the old state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 71.25,
          "en": "because this state update is scheduled by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.25,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "And in the end it will of course be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 75.51,
          "en": "pretty much instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.51,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "but it will not be executed right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "and it will not magically change this value which belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "to the old component function execution, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 87.42,
          "en": "Instead, this will trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.42,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "a new component function execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 91.77,
          "en": "and the new state will be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 94.053,
          "en": "the next time this executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.97,
          "en": "But because those state updates are scheduled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.97,
          "end": 103.97,
          "en": "it is considered a best practice to perform state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 109.1,
          "en": "that depend on the old state value using this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 111.75999999999999,
          "en": "which I also showed you before in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 117.36,
          "en": "where you pass a function to the state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.36,
          "end": 121.38,
          "en": "and that function then receives the old state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 124.86,
          "en": "and should return the new state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.86,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "And you can use the old state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 129.153,
          "en": "to then derive the new snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "Because when using this approach here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "React guarantees you that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "you will always get the latest state snapshot available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 142.59,
          "en": "and if multiple state updates of the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.59,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "should be scheduled, they will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.81,
          "en": "in the order in which they were scheduled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.81,
          "end": 151.14,
          "en": "And you will always get the right value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "For example, here, if for some reason I decided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 159.06,
          "en": "that I then wanna update my chosenCount here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.06,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "by adding one to it, we would get a strange result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 165.06,
          "en": "if we try to do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "If we set the chosenCount to the newCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 169.683,
          "en": "and we then add one to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "Since I'm using my old state like this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "I will not get newCount plus one as a result of this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "but instead my old state plus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "So if I do that and I click 10 here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 188.22,
          "en": "I get one as a new initial count value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.22,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "because the one here was added to my old chosenCount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 192.783,
          "en": "which was zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.34,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "If instead we used this function form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "where we get the previous chosenCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 204.98,
          "en": "passed in automatically by React, and we then add one to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "we would get the newCount plus one instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "because now both state updates are scheduled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 214.74,
          "en": "and they're guaranteed to be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 218.01,
          "en": "in the order in which they are scheduled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.01,
          "end": 219.96,
          "en": "But now the second state update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.96,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "will then get the latest state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 226.62,
          "en": "at the point of time where this scheduled update is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.62,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "and therefore it will get that newCount value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 232.383,
          "en": "that was set by this state update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "So now if we change the code like this and save this, reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 240.603,
          "en": "and enter 10 here, for example, we get 11 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 245.52,
          "en": "And this is an important mechanism to be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.52,
          "end": 247.44,
          "en": "and you should especially keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.44,
          "end": 250.5,
          "en": "that you can't use the new state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 252.78,
          "en": "right after setting it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.78,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "This won't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 258.453,
          "en": "at least not as you might expect it to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 264.06,
          "en": "Now what's all important to know about this state scheduling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.06,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "is that if you have multiple state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "that are in the end triggered simultaneously",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "so in the same function here, you will not end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 278.82,
          "en": "with multiple component function executions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.82,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "because that would of course be pretty inefficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 285.3,
          "en": "But technically this is of course what could happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.3,
          "end": 289.71,
          "en": "if React wouldn't take care for it not to happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.71,
          "end": 292.08,
          "en": "because technically we're calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.08,
          "end": 294.9,
          "en": "two state updating functions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.9,
          "end": 297.27,
          "en": "And therefore, technically since you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.27,
          "end": 300.57,
          "en": "that executing such a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 300.57,
          "end": 303.54,
          "en": "triggers the component function to run again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.54,
          "end": 306.93,
          "en": "you could expect the component function to run twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 306.93,
          "end": 308.853,
          "en": "because we have two state updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.99,
          "end": 312.72,
          "en": "But this is not what happens here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.72,
          "end": 317.19,
          "en": "If we open the console and clear this and enter a value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 318.45,
          "en": "and click Set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 318.45,
          "end": 322.08,
          "en": "You see the app component function is only executed once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.08,
          "end": 326.103,
          "en": "It's only called once and not a second time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.45,
          "end": 329.73,
          "en": "And that's the case because React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 329.73,
          "end": 333.12,
          "en": "also performs state batching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 336.3,
          "en": "which simply means that multiple state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.3,
          "end": 341.3,
          "en": "that are triggered from the same function, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 341.31,
          "end": 344.7,
          "en": "are batched together and will only lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 344.7,
          "end": 347.613,
          "en": "to one component function execution.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}